                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "[h1]\"A room of darkness\"[/h1]\nHotel Blind is a blind walking simulator in a way of a text adventure. You'll see nothing except a black screen. Try to find over WASD controls the East/West walls and North/South walls. There are end tables in the corners. Each furniture will be announced as a text. Before you can leave a room you have to find special objects and finish some tasks.\n\nUnfortunately the implementation of the game is ridiculous bad and inspireless. You don't even hear your own steps. Sometimes you can still walk infine into a direction without hitting a wall at all. Also I find it weird to name walls North/South and East/West as if the programmer was to lazy to distinguish between all 4 directions. Choosing the Unreal4 engine for an only black game is a joke. It could also be programmed in Unity, RPG maker or a shitty Dos engine. No requirements for high end graphics. And 800MB download for what? Unused graphic libraries? So it's like in the fable of \"The Empereor's new clothes\". You can only enjoy what you don't see.",
